  "title": "opensafety: Avoid some technically UB signed overflow",
  "description": "The usual integer promotions means that if something is supposed to\nbe unsigned, it doesn't help to make it an unsigned type of smaller\nrank than an int. In practice it doesn't save on performance either.\n\nCoverity CID 1604251\n\nAlso get rid of an unnecessary uint_format_value use.",
